var fixLoopItems = []edakit.Item{
	it(2, "A spacing violation sits between two routed signal wires. Where should an agent send it?",
		"Back to the detailed router as a rerun of that region, a Tier 1 action", []string{"To a human layout engineer to draw by hand", "To the fill step", "Nowhere; waive it"},
		"Routed metal is the router's output. Rerunning it with the violation as a blockage or penalty keeps the database consistent."),
	it(2, "A violation lies inside a hard macro supplied by an IP vendor. What should the agent do?",
		"Escalate it: the macro's layout is not the router's to change", []string{"Reroute the macro's internal wires", "Delete the macro shapes near the marker", "Add fill on top of it"},
		"Fixed IP is outside the agent's change surface; only the owner can change it or obtain a waiver."),
	it(2, "After a router update, the same minimum-area violation appears on hundreds of nets. What is the best classification?",
		"A systematic router configuration issue, fixed once in the router's rule settings rather than net by net",
		[]string{"Hundreds of independent random errors", "A density problem", "An LVS short"},
		"A pattern across many markers points to a cause upstream. One Tier 1 config fix beats hundreds of patches."),
	it(2, "Markers appear for a rule that the foundry removed in the latest deck. What should the agent check first?",
		"Which deck version the run used", []string{"The router's cost function", "The fill density", "The netlist"},
		"A stale deck produces false violations. Fixing layout for a rule that no longer exists wastes work and can harm yield."),
	it(3, "When should an agent's DRC fix be accepted?",
		"When the full signoff DRC and LVS pass and the differential run shows no new markers", []string{"When the marker it targeted disappears", "When the fast predictor reports zero hotspots", "When the router finishes without error"},
		"DRC-clean and LVS-clean are the golden tests. A local fix that adds markers elsewhere or breaks connectivity is not a fix."),
	it(3, "Why should an agent not fix routed-metal violations by editing polygons directly in the stream?",
		"Direct edits bypass the routing database, so the design database, extraction and timing no longer match the layout",
		[]string{"GDSII files cannot be edited", "Polygon edits always create shorts", "DRC cannot check edited polygons"},
		"Fixes should go through the engine that owns the data, so every downstream view stays consistent."),
	it(3, "The violation count goes 120, 40, 38, 41, 39 over five agent iterations. What should the loop do?",
		"Stop and escalate the remaining violations, since the loop has stopped converging", []string{"Keep iterating indefinitely", "Revert to the first iteration", "Waive all remaining violations"},
		"A bounded loop with a progress test avoids oscillation; the remaining hard cases go to a human."),
	it(3, "After the agent reroutes 200 nets to fix spacing, what else must be rerun before signoff?",
		"Extraction and timing, because the reroutes changed parasitics", []string{"Synthesis", "Floorplanning", "Nothing else"},
		"DRC fixes change wires, which changes RC. The ECO loop closes only when timing is clean too, with a human approving the final ECO."),
}

